{
  "id": "ss.relic.ram",
  "name": "Ram horns",
  "description": "A rhinoceros beetle's horn in profile: rooted in a dark strip of head at the bottom of the plate, rising and leaning forward to the right, thick at the base and forked at the tip, with the front face lit amber and the back face in shadow. Behind it, two short solid grey strokes of different lengths — the air it has just come through — set low and left so the horn is plainly moving forward, not standing. The relic adds knockback, and a horn thrown forward is the one insect shape whose entire job is shoving. The strokes are solid shapes and not a fade, because a translucent smear at this size is a blur; and the head is kept to a sliver so there is no face under the horn.",
